  "presentation_summary": [
    "Thirty-nine-year-old man underwent septoplasty and turbinoplasty under general anesthesia with succinylcholine, rocuronium, and desflurane exposure.",
    "At the end of surgery he developed marked hypercapnia with EtCO2 up to 130 mmHg, tachycardia, and axillary temperature 39.5 C.",
    "Initial arterial blood gas and chemistry showed severe mixed acidosis and hyperkalemia: pH 7.05, pCO2 84 mmHg, pO2 322 mmHg, bicarbonate 23.2 mmol/L, base excess -9, lactate 5.2 mmol/L, potassium 7.2 mmol/L, calcium 1.67 mmol/L, and creatinine 150 umol/L.",
    "ICU course included myoglobinuria, severe hypoglycemia, persistent acidosis, very high CK peaking above 100000 U/L, LDH and transaminase elevation, hypoxemia at 24 hours, and persistent renal/electrolyte abnormalities.",
    "Desflurane was stopped and he was treated with cooling, dantrolene 250 mg IV, non-triggering anesthesia, bladder catheterization, diuretics, temperature monitoring, electrolyte/acidosis correction, insulin-dextrose, and serum therapy.",
    "He was extubated at 24 hours and left ICU at 48 hours."
  ],
